(7699659, 1263422, 181847, '<td valign="top">Thank you all for your votes and comments. <br/> <br/>This photo has quickly became one of my all time favorites. It was recently featured in Landscape Photography Magazine Issue #126 Last Light Assignment. <br/> <br/>There is a high resolution full screen virtual tour you can view on my website. As this site doesn''t allow for posting url''s search for Abbas Creations Photography. You will find the image in the Wall Murals pull down menu. Click on the photo to go to a details page describing the photo. Clicking on the photo on the details page will launch the virtual tour.</td>', 'Thank you all for your votes and comments.  This photo has quickly became one of my all time favorites. It was recently featured in Landscape Photography Magazine Issue #126 Last Light Assignment.  There is a high resolution full screen virtual tour you can view on my website. As this site doesn''t allow for posting url''s search for Abbas Creations Photography. You will find the image in the Wall Murals pull down menu. Click on the photo to go to a details page describing the photo. Clicking on the photo on the details page will launch the virtual tour.', '2021-08-25 14:04:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(7699661, 1263422, 181847, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe:</b></div><hr/><i> Congrats!<br/>70?!!  Not being a landscape shooter Im too lazy to even do a 3-5 focus stack. Wonder how many others here in our drastically dwindling herd go to such lengths. Impressive. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This image is not a focus stacked shot. However I often do focus stacked wall murals I recently finished one that is a focus stacked image consisting of 1864 individual images to yield 120 focus stacked images in an 8 row x 16 column array resulting in a 12 ft. x 15-1/2 ft. wall mural. 2.5 Giga-pixels, 43,829 x 56,987 pixels, 146" x 190" 300 dpi My profile has my website url. It is in the Wall Murals group under Galleries tab titled Crystal Mill.</td>', 'Originally posted by oldbimmercoupe: Congrats!70?!!  Not being a landscape shooter Im too lazy to even do a 3-5 focus stack. Wonder how many others here in our drastically dwindling herd go to such lengths. Impressive.   This image is not a focus stacked shot. However I often do focus stacked wall murals I recently finished one that is a focus stacked image consisting of 1864 individual images to yield 120 focus stacked images in an 8 row x 16 column array resulting in a 12 ft. x 15-1/2 ft. wall mural. 2.5 Giga-pixels, 43,829 x 56,987 pixels, 146" x 190" 300 dpi My profile has my website url. It is in the Wall Murals group under Galleries tab titled Crystal Mill.', '2021-08-25 16:10:06.000000', NULL, 0),
